# Publication font settings

This chapter owns `src/publication-settings.ts` and its headless tests. It reads
only root `index.literate` SETTINGS tokens from a `ParsedProject`; `parseProject`
has already canonicalized paths with `safeRelativePath`. Chapter settings and
unrelated keys (including theme) are not ours. Keys and `on`/`off` are case-sensitive.

Code defaults to Lilex Nerd Font, whose regular, bold, italic and bold-italic
files all report that exact family via `fc-scan`. Native italic faces avoid
requiring synthesis for the default code comments.

This is font selection, **not font bundling**. There is no filesystem access,
font lookup, global installation, or runtime dependency. Renderers remain
responsible for applying the selected families and ligature policy. In particular,
`off` calls for disabling `calt` (`-calt`), verified for the actual D2 font, rather
than merely disabling `liga`. This chapter does not change a renderer or CLI.


## Public contract

All five families are resolved strings. Omitted notes inherit the final selected
body family, whereas fragments default independently to Monofur. Diagnostics
here describe settings only: they do not copy `project.diagnostics`. Callers must
still gate rendering on source diagnostics through preparation (`preparePandoc`);
a settings result alone is not permission to render. Source NUL rejection belongs
to the existing parser, before Markdown can replace NUL with a replacement glyph.

```ts : <<publication settings contract>>=
import type { GenerationDiagnostic, ParsedProject } from './engine';

export interface PublicationFonts {
    body: string;
    heading: string;
    code: string;
    fragment: string;
    note: string;
}
export interface PublicationSettingsResult {
    fonts: PublicationFonts;
    codeLigatures: boolean;
    diagnostics: GenerationDiagnostic[];
}
```

## Scan in authored order

Each call starts fresh. A missing root is valid and yields defaults. We consume
the existing fence tokens, including fences inside Markdown containers, without
reparsing source or treating ordinary code blocks as settings.

```ts : <<publication settings resolver>>=
export function resolvePublicationSettings(project: ParsedProject): PublicationSettingsResult {
    const fonts: PublicationFonts = {
        body: 'Latin Modern Roman', heading: 'Monofur Nerd Font',
        code: 'Lilex Nerd Font', fragment: 'Monofur Nerd Font', note: ''
    };
    let codeLigatures = true;
    let explicitNote = false;
    const diagnostics: GenerationDiagnostic[] = [];
    const document = project.documents.find(value => value.path === 'index.literate');
    for (const token of document?.tokens ?? []) {
        if (token.type !== 'fence' || token.info.trim() !== 'SETTINGS') { continue; }
        token.content.split('\n').forEach((line: string, index: number) => {
            const match = /^\s*(font-body|font-heading|font-code|font-fragment|font-note|font-code-ligatures)\s*=(.*)$/.exec(line);
            if (!match) { return; }
            const key = match[1];
            const value = match[2].trim();
```

Family values use the same simple ASCII grammar as the existing LaTeX `fontName`:
1–100 letters, digits, spaces, dots or hyphens, starting with a letter or digit.
Whitespace around values is trimmed; empty names, paths and TeX syntax are rejected.
Last valid wins, but every invalid occurrence remains a diagnostic, just as for
theme settings. Coordinates are zero-based: the fence map starts at its opener,
so content line zero is source line `map[0] + 1`, also within lists and quotes.

```ts : <<publication settings resolver>>=+
            const report = (message: string): void => {
                diagnostics.push({ path: document!.path,
                    line: (token.map?.[0] ?? 0) + index + 1, column: 0, message });
            };
            if (key === 'font-code-ligatures') {
                if (value === 'on' || value === 'off') { codeLigatures = value === 'on'; }
                else { report(`Invalid ${key}: expected on or off`); }
            } else if (/^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9 .-]{0,99}$/.test(value)) {
                const role = key.slice(5) as keyof PublicationFonts;
                fonts[role] = value;
                if (role === 'note') { explicitNote = true; }
            } else {
                report(`Invalid ${key}: font must be a simple family name (1–100 ASCII characters)`);
            }
        });
    }
    if (!explicitNote) { fonts.note = fonts.body; }
    return { fonts, codeLigatures, diagnostics };
}
```

The generated settings regression implementation is collected in
[Appendix H — Testing and verification reference](appendix_testing_verification.html).
